Z||000013||Raydar||07-09-2001||11:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>Big shortage of your types in Australia. Wages are pretty good too   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Expect about $50 to $100 an hour or about $25 to $50 US<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not too shabby! What's the cost of living / housing in Aus?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||07-09-2001||11:21 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 8Ball:<BR><B>Thanks and how's the rent in atlanta? Pretty high?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Depends on where you want to live. In town, condos go for about $240K.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>Needless to say, I don't live in town.<P>You can get a new house in the 'burbs for around $120K. Older houses are a little cheaper and probably built a little better, if you can find one. There ARE some bargains to be found, but you've gotta know where to look. And where NOT to look. These prices are for stuff that's about a 20-30 mile drive from downtown Atl. (That's about average commute distance, here.) <P>Apartment rent is around $700-$1k/mo. I think. Been a while since I rented, though. Probably some cheaper stuff too. Houses are more, of course. I can poke around my area and see what I can find, if these prices haven't scared you off.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
